WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.745
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:18.015 --> 00:20.485
(Kang Hoon, Cho Hyun Chul, Kim Jeong Jin)

3
00:23.715 --> 00:25.725
(Lee E Dam, Moon Hee, Yoon Ga I)

4
00:33.625 --> 00:35.165
(Jeon Bae Soo, Lee Seo Hwan, Oh Eui Sik)

5
00:55.085 --> 00:57.454
(Happy Anding)

6
00:57.455 --> 00:59.124
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

7
00:59.125 --> 01:00.354
(All people, groups, firms, places, and events are fictional.)

8
01:00.355 --> 01:01.554
(Child actors were filmed safely with their guardians present.)

9
01:01.555 --> 01:02.754
(Animal scenes were staged under welfare rules.)

10
01:02.755 --> 01:03.955
(AI-based technology was used in parts of the production.)

11
01:23.115 --> 01:24.585
- Gosh! - Gosh, you scared me!

12
01:25.715 --> 01:26.815
- Who is that? - What's going on?

13
01:27.145 --> 01:28.215
Who's that?

14
01:28.785 --> 01:29.785
What's going on?

15
01:32.125 --> 01:33.885
- Darn it. - Hey, stop. Don't go.

16
01:33.985 --> 01:35.025
Who knows what she might do?

17
01:35.095 --> 01:36.895
- Hey. - Hey.

18
01:43.735 --> 01:44.735
I'm...

19
01:46.065 --> 01:47.365
that crazy girl.

20
02:06.885 --> 02:07.895
I'm...

21
02:09.725 --> 02:11.195
your fan.

22
02:13.225 --> 02:14.225
So please,

23
02:17.335 --> 02:18.535
don't disband.

24
02:22.375 --> 02:23.605
You can't.

25
02:24.805 --> 02:25.805
You can't disband.

26
02:54.065 --> 02:55.235
Eun Young really made a mess.

27
03:10.155 --> 03:13.525
Well, look at us all together again.

28
03:13.625 --> 03:16.555
Keep this up, and we'll be best friends. Cheers.

29
03:16.625 --> 03:18.265
All right, let's toast. Cheers.

30
03:23.595 --> 03:24.765
Wait, but...

31
03:25.535 --> 03:27.505
when you say you're a fan,

32
03:28.075 --> 03:31.605
you mean you're a fan who actually likes us, right?

33
03:32.405 --> 03:34.815
How long have you liked us?

34
03:36.845 --> 03:40.215
For about a year.

35
03:40.915 --> 03:44.285
A year? That's pretty long. A year is quite a while, isn't it?

36
03:46.085 --> 03:47.125
By the way,

37
03:48.355 --> 03:52.125
the pigeon and the drinks... Why did you do that?

38
03:55.795 --> 03:58.035
Well, about the drinks,

39
03:59.005 --> 04:00.565
I really had no idea.

40
04:01.535 --> 04:04.135
And the pigeon,

41
04:05.205 --> 04:06.505
there was a misunderstanding.

42
04:08.575 --> 04:09.745
I'm...

43
04:10.175 --> 04:13.945
I'm really sorry about that.

44
04:15.615 --> 04:19.185
Well, sure. Things happen. Yes, I totally get it.

45
04:22.025 --> 04:27.195
Can I keep asking questions? Why do you like us?

46
04:28.635 --> 04:30.695
- Pardon? - I mean, what made you...

47
04:31.165 --> 04:34.605
become a fan?

48
04:35.205 --> 04:37.635
Do you know any of our comedy sketches?

49
04:37.945 --> 04:40.475
- What's your favourite? - Hey, come on...

50
04:41.005 --> 04:45.015
Cut it out. Her face is about to burst.

51
04:45.745 --> 04:48.515
I'm sorry. It's just, this is a first for me.

52
04:48.585 --> 04:50.115
Having a fan and all.

53
04:51.055 --> 04:52.085
To start with,

54
04:52.925 --> 04:54.955
you put your whole body into it on stage.

55
04:56.425 --> 04:57.995
That's your biggest charm.

56
04:58.495 --> 05:00.495
And I love how dedicated you are to your makeup and costumes.

57
05:00.625 --> 05:03.295
Personally, the "Woman with a Twist" sketch.

58
05:03.495 --> 05:06.865
It's about a cafe part-timer, so I really resonated with it.

59
05:07.335 --> 05:09.575
It was as if it were about me.

60
05:10.405 --> 05:12.174
And of course, the sketch...

61
05:12.175 --> 05:15.115
that best captures the true identity of Asura,

62
05:15.575 --> 05:18.285
"Look here, look here." I love that one too.

63
05:23.955 --> 05:24.955
Yes.

64
05:26.125 --> 05:28.755
That's why I like you guys.

65
05:29.255 --> 05:30.325
Gosh, wait...

66
05:31.265 --> 05:33.595
You know all our sketches.

67
05:33.665 --> 05:35.865
I'm actually getting kind of choked up here.

68
05:40.265 --> 05:41.505
I'm going to ask her.

69
05:42.975 --> 05:44.645
Ask her what I'm supposed to do.

70
05:46.075 --> 05:49.345
That person has been watching us all this time,

71
05:50.675 --> 05:52.185
so she might know.

72
05:59.785 --> 06:03.925
Could I ask a question this time?

73
06:04.725 --> 06:06.195
Sure, go ahead.

74
06:08.535 --> 06:11.335
Why are you disbanding?

75
06:15.035 --> 06:19.175
Whatever the reason is, isn't this wrong?

76
06:19.475 --> 06:21.005
You have fans like me.

77
06:21.075 --> 06:25.045
To suddenly disband like this without warning,

78
06:25.315 --> 06:26.585
that's just too much.

79
06:27.245 --> 06:29.885
I'll promote your channel,

80
06:30.085 --> 06:33.885
start a fan club, and work hard. No, I'll do a great job.

81
06:34.625 --> 06:35.855
So please,

82
06:36.525 --> 06:39.895
could you reconsider?

83
06:41.025 --> 06:42.035
Please?

84
06:43.665 --> 06:44.665
Please?

85
06:45.735 --> 06:48.435
- Well... - No, we can't.

86
06:51.405 --> 06:52.645
We already decided,

87
06:53.945 --> 06:56.015
and we already announced it, so take it back? No way.

88
06:57.885 --> 06:59.045
We can't undo it.

89
06:59.945 --> 07:01.045
We won't.

90
07:03.055 --> 07:05.225
Don't cut me off like that.

91
07:05.585 --> 07:08.855
Could you please reconsider just one more time?

92
07:13.065 --> 07:14.635
Let's go. I'm tired.

93
07:15.335 --> 07:18.364
- You can't just leave like this. - Eun Young!

94
07:18.365 --> 07:20.235
You can at least think about it once.

95
07:20.365 --> 07:23.204
- Let go of this. - No, just once.

96
07:23.205 --> 07:24.205
- No. - Hey.

97
07:24.275 --> 07:25.704
You're stretching my shirt.

98
07:25.705 --> 07:27.705
- Eun Young, take it easy. - What's your problem?

99
07:27.805 --> 07:29.845
Please, just this once.

100
07:29.915 --> 07:32.144
- Shall we toast? Cheers. - What's wrong with you?

101
07:32.145 --> 07:33.145
Okay.

102
07:33.146 --> 07:34.955
(Episode 3: Lunatic vs. Lunatic)

103
07:35.085 --> 07:36.185
It's fine.

104
07:39.455 --> 07:41.755
Man, we actually had a fan.

105
07:41.955 --> 07:43.825
She wasn't a crazy girl. She was a super fan.

106
07:44.225 --> 07:45.395
She's crazy too.

107
07:45.565 --> 07:46.565
Don't leave. Let go. What's wrong?

108
07:46.625 --> 07:47.795
- Let go. What's wrong? - Easy there.

109
07:47.935 --> 07:49.235
And what was with the pigeon?

110
07:51.735 --> 07:53.165
What about it? It can happen.

111
07:53.705 --> 07:54.905
She said she thought we needed it.

112
07:55.705 --> 07:57.705
The fact that she connects with you means she's not normal.

113
07:57.775 --> 08:00.175
First off, if her favourite sketch is "Look here, look here"...

114
08:00.475 --> 08:01.945
then she's definitely not normal.

115
08:02.445 --> 08:04.785
Even I'm too embarrassed to show that sketch to anyone.

116
08:05.685 --> 08:06.984
Hey, you're embarrassed?

117
08:06.985 --> 08:09.754
Should parents really be ashamed of their own child?

118
08:09.755 --> 08:10.785
Nonsense.

119
08:10.855 --> 08:13.055
Is that why every time we performed that,

120
08:13.085 --> 08:14.795
you secretly wore a mask all by yourself?

121
08:15.555 --> 08:16.955
It was the concept, you idiot. The concept.

122
08:17.195 --> 08:20.095
- The concept, you idiot. - Concept, my foot.

123
08:20.195 --> 08:21.195
What, you punk?

124
08:22.595 --> 08:25.605
Still, there was at least one person.

125
08:29.875 --> 08:31.605
Someone who told us not to quit.

126
08:42.885 --> 08:43.885
Yes.

127
08:45.055 --> 08:46.425
It wasn't a total waste of time.

128
08:50.625 --> 08:52.695
Let's wash up and sleep. I'm beat.

129
08:58.305 --> 09:02.204
I'm sorry, I'm so sorry. I tried to leave as fast as I could,

130
09:02.205 --> 09:04.175
but clueless Manager Kim...

131
09:06.075 --> 09:07.105
Na Yeon.

132
09:17.955 --> 09:19.155
Na Yeon, guess what? We have a fan.

133
09:22.325 --> 09:23.355
A fan?

134
09:28.595 --> 09:29.735
What kind of fan?

135
09:31.935 --> 09:34.004
My goodness. She brought that pigeon...

136
09:34.005 --> 09:35.175
all because of us.

137
09:35.535 --> 09:38.504
Since she did it out of love as a fan,

138
09:38.505 --> 09:40.145
it's not like we can get mad at her.

139
09:40.205 --> 09:44.145
Seriously, is this how stars feel when they have a die-hard fan?

140
09:45.345 --> 09:46.585
Look at you, Kim Nam Il.

141
09:47.585 --> 09:48.655
Are you that happy?

142
09:48.915 --> 09:50.355
Yes, I am.

143
09:52.085 --> 09:53.825
It means there's at least one person...

144
09:53.855 --> 09:55.025
who will remember us.

145
09:57.895 --> 09:59.395
Is it completely decided, then?

146
10:00.625 --> 10:01.635
Disbanding?

147
10:02.795 --> 10:03.795
Yes.

148
10:05.165 --> 10:06.665
Is it because of me?

149
10:08.335 --> 10:10.035
Because of our fight the other day?

150
10:13.575 --> 10:16.415
No, we should've done this long ago.

151
10:17.445 --> 10:19.015
We were just being foolish, clinging on.

152
10:19.715 --> 10:21.085
And you were the only one suffering.

153
10:21.485 --> 10:24.385
- Nam Il, I... - Na Yeon, I'm going to get a job.

154
10:26.685 --> 10:30.154
- A job? - I think it's time for me...

155
10:30.155 --> 10:31.395
to look for real work.

156
10:32.995 --> 10:35.235
Don't you think I'd be good at something like sales?

157
10:36.165 --> 10:37.395
You know I have a way with words.

158
10:40.105 --> 10:41.205
Well,

159
10:41.875 --> 10:45.745
as long as you're happy, I'm happy.

160
10:46.675 --> 10:47.675
Right?

161
10:49.815 --> 10:51.315
Mother.

162
10:52.615 --> 10:53.615
Hello, Mother.

163
10:53.685 --> 10:54.854
- Nam Il, it's been a while. - Mom.

164
10:54.855 --> 10:57.415
Why did you buy so much? Let me carry that for you.

165
10:57.815 --> 10:59.085
It's not heavy.

166
11:00.685 --> 11:02.625
- I'm fine. - Okay.

167
11:05.365 --> 11:07.865
Nam Il was just saying he missed you, Mom.

168
11:08.195 --> 11:09.264
Come upstairs and hang out for a bit.

169
11:09.265 --> 11:11.935
Next time. We have a family gathering today.

170
11:12.605 --> 11:13.965
Your Aunt Dong Hee is coming over, remember?

171
11:14.665 --> 11:16.534
It's not like they're strangers.

172
11:16.535 --> 11:18.005
They've had dinner together before.

173
11:20.405 --> 11:22.145
Wait a second.

174
11:22.915 --> 11:24.445
Na Yeon, I'm sorry.

175
11:24.945 --> 11:26.815
I completely forgot I had something to do at the theater.

176
11:27.515 --> 11:28.515
Right now?

177
11:28.885 --> 11:31.185
Yes. I'm sorry. I think I should get going.

178
11:31.415 --> 11:32.555
I'm sorry, Mother.

179
11:33.125 --> 11:34.485
I'll get out of your way.

180
11:36.195 --> 11:37.425
Have a wonderful time.

181
11:41.365 --> 11:43.095
- Nam Il. - See you.

182
11:52.805 --> 11:54.075
What's wrong with you lately, Mom?

183
11:54.745 --> 11:55.915
What about me?

184
11:55.975 --> 11:58.045
Why are you always so cold to Nam Il?

185
11:58.345 --> 11:59.785
You used to adore him.

186
12:00.545 --> 12:02.685
You said you liked how cheerful and affectionate he was.

187
12:02.785 --> 12:05.525
That was then, and this is now. That's exactly why I dislike him.

188
12:07.925 --> 12:09.054
What?

189
12:09.055 --> 12:11.895
He's 34 and cluelessly cheerful with no plan, which I hate.

190
12:12.425 --> 12:14.025
And even when I give him the cold shoulder,

191
12:14.625 --> 12:16.665
he just smiles and clings to me all sweet like that,

192
12:16.935 --> 12:17.995
which I hate even more.

193
12:19.705 --> 12:21.165
Are you really going to marry him?

194
12:23.675 --> 12:25.545
Yes, I am.

195
12:25.745 --> 12:27.105
If it's not him, I'm not marrying anyone.

196
12:27.705 --> 12:28.945
Unbelievable.

197
12:29.875 --> 12:31.175
I can't stand by and watch this anymore.

198
12:31.245 --> 12:33.715
- I really want you two to break up. - Mom.

199
12:33.785 --> 12:35.455
He should at least have a real job.

200
12:36.055 --> 12:37.885
An unknown comedian? My goodness.

201
12:38.385 --> 12:41.355
- That's his job. - He said he was quitting anyway.

202
12:41.525 --> 12:43.755
He's quitting comedy and getting a regular job.

203
12:45.825 --> 12:47.665
So please, stop being like this.

204
12:48.735 --> 12:50.065
Nam Il is trying his best too.

205
12:56.635 --> 12:57.835
Darn it...

206
12:58.075 --> 13:00.545
Well, looking at your test results,

207
13:01.275 --> 13:04.045
and considering how the pain flared up again out of nowhere...

208
13:05.215 --> 13:08.885
Has anything been troubling you or stressing you out lately?

209
13:09.415 --> 13:10.455
No.

210
13:12.285 --> 13:13.655
No, nothing like that at all.

211
13:14.555 --> 13:18.325
Emotional distress can manifest as physical pain.

212
13:18.795 --> 13:22.995
Please remember that managing stress is more important than medication.

213
13:26.035 --> 13:27.535
All right, we'll see you at your next appointment.

214
13:27.705 --> 13:28.805
Take care.

215
13:28.875 --> 13:31.605
(Hyujung Mental Health Clinic)

216
13:37.945 --> 13:39.444
(Did you get home safe? Are you at the venue?)

217
13:39.445 --> 13:40.945
(Call when you're free.)

218
13:47.425 --> 13:48.595
Surprise.

219
13:53.365 --> 13:55.295
What's with that reaction?

220
13:59.005 --> 14:00.005
What?

221
14:00.835 --> 14:01.835
Is something wrong?

222
14:02.335 --> 14:03.535
You scared the crap out of me, punk.

223
14:03.705 --> 14:04.905
You scared me half to death, you bastard.

224
14:05.005 --> 14:06.045
Hey!

225
14:06.305 --> 14:07.305
Come here.

226
14:09.215 --> 14:11.445
- Come here. - Seriously?

227
14:13.715 --> 14:15.355
Ignoring my texts? You just blew me off.

228
14:16.015 --> 14:17.685
How dare you leave your brother on read?

229
14:18.985 --> 14:20.085
Goodbye, everyone.

230
14:20.425 --> 14:22.325
- Open the door, you jerk. - All right!

231
14:22.595 --> 14:24.195
Hey, after running off like that the other night,

232
14:24.255 --> 14:26.525
you should've at least texted me to let me know you got home safe.

233
14:26.825 --> 14:27.865
That's rich.

234
14:28.125 --> 14:30.965
- Since when do I report to you? - Get over here. Come here.

235
14:31.635 --> 14:32.665
Not again, cut it out.

236
14:41.545 --> 14:43.015
I couldn't sleep a wink that night.

237
14:45.315 --> 14:47.145
I called you out trying to cheer you up,

238
14:48.655 --> 14:50.355
and I was worried I just made you feel worse.

239
14:54.055 --> 14:55.295
You selfish brat.

240
14:59.995 --> 15:01.025
Whatever.

241
15:01.895 --> 15:04.665
Is it anything new that Dad chewed me out?

242
15:05.835 --> 15:07.905
Besides, everything he said was true anyway.

243
15:13.145 --> 15:14.145
Hyun Gu.

244
15:14.845 --> 15:16.175
I'm quitting comedy.

245
15:17.945 --> 15:18.945
What?

246
15:19.915 --> 15:21.285
We announced our disbandment yesterday,

247
15:22.055 --> 15:23.555
and now I'm going to wrap things up for good.

248
15:31.355 --> 15:33.695
- Because of Dad? - No.

249
15:36.595 --> 15:38.565
- Because of me? - What are you talking about?

250
15:38.635 --> 15:41.805
- Then why? Why are you doing this? - There's no money in it.

251
15:42.605 --> 15:45.305
I'm sick of starving while pretending I'm winning at life.

252
15:45.645 --> 15:47.445
And it's not even fun anymore like it used to be.

253
15:48.075 --> 15:49.515
I just want to quit and make some real money.

254
15:51.575 --> 15:52.845
I'm going to get rich.

255
15:53.715 --> 15:54.715
Unbelievable...

256
15:57.455 --> 15:58.985
You tell Dad for me.

257
15:59.955 --> 16:01.585
Seeing how happy he would be...

258
16:02.525 --> 16:04.095
would make me sick to my stomach,

259
16:05.055 --> 16:06.725
so I really can't tell him myself.

260
16:20.605 --> 16:22.375
- Dad. - Hey.

261
16:22.415 --> 16:24.645
- I'm back. - Back already?

262
16:25.485 --> 16:27.884
I was going to pick you up as soon as I finished this.

263
16:27.885 --> 16:29.355
The appointment finished early.

264
16:29.915 --> 16:31.255
Tae Gu came to pick me up.

265
16:32.625 --> 16:35.225
Oh, really? That's a surprise.

266
16:36.395 --> 16:37.495
You must be tired.

267
16:39.465 --> 16:40.565
Let's go in and eat.

268
16:41.225 --> 16:42.265
Dad.

269
16:46.435 --> 16:48.065
Tae Gu says he's quitting comedy.

270
16:50.605 --> 16:54.175
He gave me all kinds of reasons, but it just sounded like nonsense.

271
16:56.715 --> 16:58.045
Something must have happened.

272
16:59.615 --> 17:00.815
Unbelievable.

273
17:01.955 --> 17:04.015
After digging his heels in all this time...

274
17:05.755 --> 17:06.825
Good for him.

275
17:07.555 --> 17:09.225
What a huge relief.

276
17:12.065 --> 17:13.125
Do you mean that?

277
17:15.635 --> 17:17.395
Is it really just a relief to you?

278
17:22.005 --> 17:23.835
Tae Gu takes after you so much.

279
17:27.105 --> 17:29.545
Finish packing up and come inside. I'll get dinner ready.

280
17:45.265 --> 17:46.425
Let's try it.

281
17:51.465 --> 17:53.105
Aren't you going to tell your family...

282
17:53.235 --> 17:54.465
that you're quitting comedy?

283
17:55.805 --> 17:57.035
My whole family is right here.

284
17:57.575 --> 18:00.075
The guys and you, boss.

285
18:04.815 --> 18:06.085
(Landlord)

286
18:06.715 --> 18:08.385
Boss, let me take this call real quick.

287
18:08.445 --> 18:10.385
- Work on this for a bit. - Okay.

288
18:14.955 --> 18:16.255
It's such a shame, isn't it?

289
18:17.625 --> 18:21.325
He dropped out of medical school and cut ties with his family.

290
18:23.095 --> 18:24.665
Look at him now.

291
18:25.235 --> 18:28.265
They say a single choice can determine your whole life.

292
18:31.235 --> 18:33.275
Why are you skewering the green onion first?

293
18:33.975 --> 18:34.975
It doesn't matter.

294
18:35.045 --> 18:36.375
What do you mean it doesn't matter?

295
18:36.445 --> 18:38.715
One quick decision ruins the whole flavour.

296
18:38.785 --> 18:41.485
A skewer has to start with meat and end with meat.

297
18:44.315 --> 18:45.985
You always pick on me, seriously.

298
18:46.425 --> 18:48.525
Hello, ma'am. I sent yesterday's rent.

299
18:48.595 --> 18:50.425
I saw that,

300
18:50.855 --> 18:52.765
but you know the lease is up soon, right?

301
18:52.825 --> 18:54.025
What do you want to do?

302
18:57.935 --> 19:00.264
- We want to renew it, of course. - Then you know you'll have to...

303
19:00.265 --> 19:02.275
pay a bit more rent this time, right?

304
19:02.835 --> 19:04.105
How much?

305
19:06.945 --> 19:07.945
Yes.

306
19:08.845 --> 19:11.745
Understood, yes. I'll talk it over with the guys.

307
19:14.245 --> 19:15.355
We're here.

308
19:16.185 --> 19:17.955
- Hey. - Welcome.

309
19:18.585 --> 19:20.525
Didn't you just eat with Na Yeon?

310
19:21.185 --> 19:23.625
I did, but I'm suddenly starving again.

311
19:28.095 --> 19:29.095
All right, look.

312
19:30.795 --> 19:31.795
What's that?

313
19:32.165 --> 19:33.605
Our list of things to wrap up.

314
19:34.635 --> 19:37.275
- Wrap up what? - The payouts from our last shows,

315
19:37.335 --> 19:38.805
the car, and the place. We have to clear it all out.

316
19:39.675 --> 19:40.675
What?

317
19:41.305 --> 19:42.645
Why are you surprised?

318
19:42.845 --> 19:45.175
We bought the car for out-of-town gigs,

319
19:45.385 --> 19:46.945
so selling it makes sense. And the place...

320
19:47.015 --> 19:48.285
Wait, but about the place...

321
19:48.345 --> 19:50.615
Just because we're disbanding doesn't mean we have to split up.

322
19:52.055 --> 19:53.555
We don't have to live together either.

323
19:53.785 --> 19:57.195
We don't know where we'll get jobs, so why stay crammed together...

324
19:57.325 --> 19:58.525
near this expensive broadcasting station?

325
19:59.565 --> 20:02.965
We'll need money to start fresh. Better clear everything out...

326
20:03.035 --> 20:04.695
and split whatever cash we can get.

327
20:05.335 --> 20:06.335
Hey.

328
20:06.465 --> 20:08.705
How much was our security deposit again?

329
20:10.535 --> 20:13.645
- It's 20,000 dollars. - 20,000 dollars...

330
20:13.805 --> 20:16.815
The lease ends around the same time as our final show,

331
20:17.745 --> 20:19.115
so we can get it back then.

332
20:19.885 --> 20:20.885
Okay.

333
20:21.415 --> 20:22.515
"Okay"?

334
20:22.985 --> 20:24.515
You're starting to hurt my feelings.

335
20:24.955 --> 20:25.955
Come on.

336
20:26.085 --> 20:28.285
Did you plan on living with me forever?

337
20:28.725 --> 20:29.755
Well, no...

338
20:31.595 --> 20:32.595
Oh, right.

339
20:32.665 --> 20:33.995
Didn't you have something to discuss?

340
20:36.335 --> 20:37.465
It's nothing.

341
20:39.735 --> 20:42.435
Over here. Come on in, hurry.

342
20:42.505 --> 20:44.035
Run, run, run!

343
20:48.205 --> 20:49.445
What's up?

344
20:51.075 --> 20:52.645
Hey, guys!

345
20:54.215 --> 20:55.885
Welcome to Korea.

346
20:57.585 --> 20:58.955
Where should we sit?

347
20:59.885 --> 21:03.255
You guys are here too? Sir, do you have tables for 20?

348
21:03.555 --> 21:05.664
Yes. Okay.

349
21:05.665 --> 21:07.865
Okay! All right. Let's go.

350
21:11.265 --> 21:15.975
One, two, three! Spread your wings wide!

351
21:16.235 --> 21:19.705
Fly freely through the sky!

352
21:19.775 --> 21:23.275
Singing and dancing

353
21:23.345 --> 21:26.815
I'm a beautiful butterfly!

354
21:27.415 --> 21:29.915
Man, it's not even Halloween. What's with this vibe?

355
21:29.985 --> 21:31.585
I can't deal with this right now.

356
21:31.915 --> 21:34.185
What's this, Los Angeles or something?

357
21:34.655 --> 21:36.055
We can hang out here for a bit, right?

358
21:36.125 --> 21:38.455
Excuse me, miss. Could you please explain...

359
21:38.525 --> 21:40.295
what's going on here?

360
21:40.665 --> 21:44.065
Plans overlapped, so I just brought everyone together.

361
21:44.165 --> 21:46.405
It's more fun with a crowd.

362
21:47.105 --> 21:49.675
I'm an introvert. This is draining my energy.

363
21:50.305 --> 21:54.045
- Man Sik is a great singer. - Sounds like a dying pig.

364
21:55.105 --> 21:58.245
Dodging the spiderwebs, I fly...

365
21:59.045 --> 22:01.585
Sorry about yesterday.

366
22:01.945 --> 22:05.355
- My sister was really in shock. - No, no, it's fine.

367
22:05.415 --> 22:09.355
I don't know about him, but I took it as a good experience.

368
22:09.425 --> 22:11.325
When else would I go through something like that?

369
22:11.395 --> 22:13.825
- I looked at the bright side. - An experience?

370
22:16.095 --> 22:19.005
You don't think this is all over, do you?

371
22:22.805 --> 22:25.475
Oh, you poor guys. What are we going to do?

372
22:27.605 --> 22:30.875
Listen carefully, guys.

373
22:31.875 --> 22:34.485
I bet I look crazy to you, right?

374
22:35.485 --> 22:38.315
Well, the real deal is my sister.

375
22:38.925 --> 22:41.155
If I'm just acting, she's the real deal.

376
22:41.225 --> 22:43.295
A bona fide lunatic.

377
22:45.695 --> 22:48.865
- She doesn't seem like that type. - She seems normal usually.

378
22:48.935 --> 22:51.294
Gentle, cute.

379
22:51.295 --> 22:54.865
But once she snaps,

380
22:54.965 --> 22:56.905
she sees things through to the bitter end.

381
22:57.775 --> 22:59.805
She has this look in her eyes.

382
23:05.545 --> 23:07.945
That subtly unhinged look focused on its target.

383
23:08.245 --> 23:11.655
So innocent, yet so chilling.

384
23:31.305 --> 23:33.045
That was when I knew for sure.

385
23:33.405 --> 23:36.415
My sister isn't normal.

386
23:46.355 --> 23:48.895
Eun Young! What's this?

387
23:48.955 --> 23:50.095
Eun Young!

388
23:57.365 --> 23:58.535
I got it...

389
24:00.205 --> 24:01.205
What?

390
24:05.075 --> 24:09.545
Once she gets that look? It only ends when someone bleeds.

391
24:09.845 --> 24:10.975
Hey.

392
24:14.045 --> 24:16.585
Can you lend me some cash? Just five dollars.

393
24:16.655 --> 24:17.715
I'll pay you right back tomorrow.

394
24:20.185 --> 24:23.095
Yes! Hey, gather the others. Let's go.

395
24:24.095 --> 24:25.095
Nice one.

396
24:27.465 --> 24:28.465
My five dollars.

397
24:28.795 --> 24:31.035
I forgot. I'll give it to you later.

398
24:32.965 --> 24:33.965
When later?

399
24:34.465 --> 24:36.335
I said I'll give it to you.

400
24:36.675 --> 24:38.775
Stop annoying me over five lousy dollars.

401
24:42.945 --> 24:43.945
Darn it.

402
24:45.445 --> 24:46.445
Five dollars.

403
24:48.515 --> 24:49.585
How much is it?

404
24:53.225 --> 24:56.555
- Five dollars. - Just give it to her.

405
24:56.625 --> 24:58.825
- Give it to her already. - Five dollars.

406
24:59.095 --> 25:02.435
Seriously. She has a death wish.

407
25:05.065 --> 25:08.335
Or until they're bled completely dry.

408
25:09.775 --> 25:11.375
Oh, come on.

409
25:11.535 --> 25:14.345
- You're exaggerating a bit. - I'm serious.

410
25:14.405 --> 25:16.115
Even with me running my mouth like this,

411
25:16.175 --> 25:18.174
I've never been beaten up once.

412
25:18.175 --> 25:21.045
Even the school bullies shivered at the mention of my sister's name.

413
25:21.615 --> 25:22.655
If you mess with her,

414
25:24.215 --> 25:25.315
you're screwed.

415
25:26.155 --> 25:27.155
And...

416
25:27.985 --> 25:29.325
yesterday,

417
25:30.255 --> 25:33.595
I saw that look again.

418
25:35.325 --> 25:36.335
Have a good day.

419
25:38.065 --> 25:39.705
So...

420
25:40.235 --> 25:42.065
are you telling us to be careful?

421
25:42.265 --> 25:44.575
I mean, thanks for the concern,

422
25:44.975 --> 25:47.075
but we're not exactly pushovers either.

423
25:47.845 --> 25:48.845
Especially...

424
25:49.345 --> 25:51.915
this guy. He isn't your average nutjob.

425
25:52.545 --> 25:53.545
Darn it.

426
26:00.085 --> 26:01.085
Hold on.

427
26:02.325 --> 26:03.595
Drinks are on me today.

428
26:36.625 --> 26:41.865
(Daeim International Co., Ltd. Go Eun Young)

429
27:00.385 --> 27:01.385
Who is it?

430
27:05.085 --> 27:06.625
- Good morning. - Goodness.

431
27:07.685 --> 27:10.355
I made sure to check the expiration date this time.

432
27:11.755 --> 27:14.065
You're not disbanding, right?

433
27:15.895 --> 27:18.135
That subtly unhinged look focused on its target.

434
27:18.195 --> 27:21.435
So innocent, yet so chilling.

435
27:31.515 --> 27:33.245
(Asura)

436
27:34.745 --> 27:36.455
(Against)

437
27:39.225 --> 27:40.955
(Disbandment)

438
27:42.695 --> 27:44.025
It's on the house.

439
27:49.565 --> 27:51.095
Hey, Tae Gu. Hey...

440
27:51.595 --> 27:54.035
Hey, that's hot. Hey, doesn't that burn?

441
27:59.575 --> 28:00.705
You ruthless bastard.

442
28:01.705 --> 28:03.975
Would you like another cup?

443
28:07.145 --> 28:08.145
Guys.

444
28:10.085 --> 28:11.085
We're sold out.

445
28:11.585 --> 28:12.625
What?

446
28:12.755 --> 28:13.825
We sold out.

447
28:15.955 --> 28:17.955
- Sold out? - Yes, completely.

448
28:24.335 --> 28:26.565
- Is this free? - Yes.

449
28:27.765 --> 28:30.405
Please leave a review after watching the show.

450
28:30.735 --> 28:32.705
- Okay. - Thank you.

451
28:50.195 --> 28:53.195
(Asura's Tenth Anniversary Special Show)

452
29:07.505 --> 29:10.045
(Comedy Town)

453
29:10.115 --> 29:12.885
(Asura's Tenth Anniversary Show)

454
29:19.385 --> 29:22.055
I waited so I could apologize.

455
29:22.595 --> 29:25.695
I just wanted to cheer you up.

456
29:27.525 --> 29:28.925
If I upset you,

457
29:30.295 --> 29:31.295
I'm truly...

458
29:32.435 --> 29:35.405
- sorry. - You don't need to apologize.

459
29:35.465 --> 29:36.475
It's okay.

460
29:48.115 --> 29:49.115
Sure, well...

461
29:50.755 --> 29:52.625
- I get where you're coming from... - But still.

462
29:54.885 --> 29:57.925
Could you please reconsider disbanding?

463
29:58.725 --> 30:01.225
I really hope you don't break up.

464
30:01.865 --> 30:02.865
Just once.

465
30:04.265 --> 30:06.865
Could you think it over one more time?

466
30:08.405 --> 30:09.405
Please?

467
30:12.105 --> 30:13.105
Hey, let's go.

468
30:15.805 --> 30:17.875
Hey, it's raining. Let's give her a ride.

469
30:18.175 --> 30:19.175
Hurry up.

470
30:20.215 --> 30:21.215
I'm sorry.

471
30:22.445 --> 30:23.455
Get home safe.

472
30:25.915 --> 30:27.425
- Take care. - Cold-hearted jerk.

473
30:55.215 --> 30:56.785
Didn't you take it a bit too far?

474
30:57.315 --> 30:58.315
What?

475
30:58.815 --> 31:01.225
Seriously, leaving a woman all by herself...

476
31:01.925 --> 31:03.825
in the middle of the night in the rain?

477
31:03.895 --> 31:05.695
I left her alone precisely because she's a woman.

478
31:06.195 --> 31:08.425
If she were a guy, I would've beaten the crap out of him.

479
31:09.125 --> 31:10.765
Did you really have to put it that way?

480
31:11.795 --> 31:12.805
What?

481
31:13.705 --> 31:15.005
I'm actually grateful to her.

482
31:16.705 --> 31:18.635
She's doing this because she loves our trio.

483
31:19.845 --> 31:21.605
Grateful, my foot. She's so annoying.

484
31:22.605 --> 31:24.175
Whatever. It's pissing me off, so drop it.

485
31:24.245 --> 31:27.845
You ruthless bastard. You make me sick, seriously.

486
31:31.985 --> 31:34.755
Hey, want me to cheer you guys up?

487
31:35.325 --> 31:37.995
- Guess who I met yesterday. - I couldn't care less.

488
31:40.265 --> 31:41.425
I went to see CEO Shin.

489
31:42.325 --> 31:44.295
We're getting all that gig money he stiffed us on.

490
31:45.795 --> 31:47.705
For real? That scumbag agreed to pay?

491
31:47.865 --> 31:48.865
Yes.

492
31:49.235 --> 31:51.405
I threatened to report him, and he rolled right over.

493
31:52.105 --> 31:53.245
It comes to about 4,000 dollars.

494
31:53.475 --> 31:55.975
Once we get the apartment deposit and sort everything else out,

495
31:56.215 --> 31:57.945
I think we can walk away with about 10,000 dollars each.

496
31:58.015 --> 32:00.945
Gosh. Man, that's insane.

497
32:01.015 --> 32:02.715
I thought we'd never see that money.

498
32:02.785 --> 32:04.015
- Right? - Right?

499
32:18.065 --> 32:19.065
Nice.

500
32:19.565 --> 32:21.005
The person you're calling is unavailable...

501
32:21.805 --> 32:23.935
Where on earth did she go?

502
32:48.995 --> 32:50.695
You're back?

503
32:53.035 --> 32:56.135
Eun Young! What happened to you?

504
33:01.405 --> 33:03.115
I'm so furious, seriously.

505
33:03.515 --> 33:06.245
How could they leave someone behind in this pouring rain?

506
33:07.915 --> 33:10.615
That's not what happened, I...

507
33:10.685 --> 33:12.255
Forget it. Stop taking their side. It's annoying.

508
33:13.085 --> 33:14.825
It's really not like that.

509
33:18.525 --> 33:19.525
Eun Young.

510
33:20.565 --> 33:21.795
Just stop it now.

511
33:21.925 --> 33:23.035
Even I'd hate it.

512
33:23.095 --> 33:25.195
Stopping someone who wants to quit...

513
33:26.465 --> 33:27.805
That's not cheering them on.

514
33:28.435 --> 33:29.535
That's just harassing them.

515
33:31.575 --> 33:33.405
(Asura)

516
33:37.145 --> 33:39.715
I know. I do.

517
33:40.445 --> 33:42.185
Then why are you doing this?

518
33:46.455 --> 33:47.525
Ji Young.

519
33:48.885 --> 33:49.895
I'm...

520
33:56.125 --> 33:57.135
I'm...

521
34:01.365 --> 34:02.605
I'm so cold.

522
34:07.545 --> 34:09.205
Dry your hair.

523
34:10.145 --> 34:12.115
(Soojung Villa)

524
34:12.175 --> 34:14.145
(No Unauthorized Parking)

525
34:20.025 --> 34:21.955
(Deposit: 4,000 Dollars Hwanggu Media Co., Ltd.)

526
34:27.425 --> 34:28.425
Hello.

527
34:32.935 --> 34:35.005
Looks like you're heading to your part-time job.

528
34:35.405 --> 34:37.535
- Yes. - Did you get home safely yesterday?

529
34:37.905 --> 34:39.745
- Yes. - My sister is sick.

530
34:39.805 --> 34:41.275
She got completely soaked in the rain,

531
34:41.345 --> 34:42.675
caught a summer cold, of all things,

532
34:42.745 --> 34:43.945
and now she's hovering between life and death.

533
34:44.015 --> 34:45.575
So I'm out getting medicine.

534
34:47.045 --> 34:48.945
Liquid medicine usually works better than pills.

535
34:49.755 --> 34:50.855
Get that next time.

536
35:03.365 --> 35:04.365
Hyun Kyung.

537
35:06.035 --> 35:07.765
Why do I even care?

538
35:16.645 --> 35:18.075
I'm stepping out for a bit.

539
35:18.245 --> 35:19.585
Eat your porridge and take your medicine.

540
35:56.415 --> 35:57.415
Which unit is it?

541
36:17.605 --> 36:18.635
I like you.

542
36:23.915 --> 36:25.115
What?

543
36:31.085 --> 36:32.655
What are you talking about?

544
36:39.725 --> 36:43.295
You asked me on the rooftop before. About having something I love.

545
36:44.395 --> 36:46.035
Something everyone says is wrong,

546
36:47.365 --> 36:48.965
but I can't live without.

547
36:49.035 --> 36:50.275
You asked if I had anything like that.

548
36:52.775 --> 36:55.645
For me, that's Asura.

549
36:57.415 --> 36:58.675
It's all of you.

550
37:02.485 --> 37:05.455
- Unbelievable. - So, I'm sorry, but...

551
37:07.685 --> 37:09.325
I'm not going to give up.

552
37:09.995 --> 37:11.395
Once I get better,

553
37:12.155 --> 37:13.565
I'm going to follow you around again.

554
37:14.865 --> 37:16.735
I'll keep following you relentlessly,

555
37:17.695 --> 37:18.995
bothering you,

556
37:19.935 --> 37:21.235
and driving you crazy.

557
37:23.705 --> 37:24.975
You're a lunatic...

558
37:28.745 --> 37:31.244
- You're out of your mind. - Are you angry?

559
37:31.245 --> 37:33.045
Do I look like I'm having fun right now?

560
37:39.055 --> 37:40.085
But you know,

561
37:42.125 --> 37:43.455
strangely,

562
37:44.895 --> 37:46.095
in my eyes,

563
37:48.765 --> 37:50.265
you keep looking sad.

564
37:52.095 --> 37:55.005
You don't look angry. You look sad.

565
37:58.435 --> 37:59.505
Am I wrong?

566
38:14.785 --> 38:17.155
I can't believe this.

567
38:18.595 --> 38:19.865
You really are sick.

568
38:21.525 --> 38:23.135
You're seriously sick right now.

569
38:24.765 --> 38:27.105
You must think I'm a pushover just because I hear you out,

570
38:28.235 --> 38:30.235
so stay 100 meters away from me.

571
38:30.775 --> 38:32.075
Don't talk to me,

572
38:33.505 --> 38:34.645
and don't even come near me.

573
38:35.505 --> 38:36.715
Otherwise, I really will...

574
38:39.015 --> 38:40.345
report you to the police.

575
38:55.295 --> 38:58.365
Comedy trio, Asura.

576
39:01.005 --> 39:02.005
You're back.

577
39:10.315 --> 39:13.245
What's wrong? What is it? Hey.

578
39:14.585 --> 39:15.615
What are you doing?

579
39:17.485 --> 39:21.055
Hey. Wait, hey, what are you doing?

580
39:21.525 --> 39:22.525
Hey!

581
39:27.665 --> 39:29.595
You said you would call. Why haven't you?

582
39:29.795 --> 39:32.365
If you don't answer by the weekend, I'll assume you're not renewing.

583
39:40.305 --> 39:41.805
(Glass Bottles, Cans, Scrap Metal)

584
39:54.485 --> 39:57.155
Darn it. Why is he doing that?

585
39:58.125 --> 40:00.765
Hey, that will break. Be careful. Seriously.

586
40:02.995 --> 40:03.995
Jun Seo.

587
40:04.965 --> 40:06.705
Stop him. I think he's lost his mind.

588
40:10.705 --> 40:11.705
What's he doing?

589
40:11.775 --> 40:14.174
I don't know. He came back acting like this.

590
40:14.175 --> 40:15.275
He says he's clearing things out.

591
40:15.345 --> 40:16.945
Now that we've decided, we should get it over with.

592
40:17.315 --> 40:19.045
Trash what we can trash, sell what we can sell.

593
40:19.485 --> 40:20.545
How much should I list this for?

594
40:20.885 --> 40:21.915
You're throwing that away too?

595
40:22.215 --> 40:25.485
- Hey, this is our debut outfit. - What does that matter now?

596
40:25.555 --> 40:26.555
It's over anyway.

597
40:26.755 --> 40:29.225
- It's just garbage now. - Seriously, man.

598
40:29.325 --> 40:31.225
Are you money-crazy? Just sell your own stuff, darn it.

599
40:34.265 --> 40:35.795
What's the big rush?

600
40:38.595 --> 40:39.605
Hey.

601
40:40.805 --> 40:41.805
Hey.

602
40:43.705 --> 40:44.705
Hey.

603
40:45.805 --> 40:47.575
What's the big rush?

604
40:59.455 --> 41:01.555
As soon as we decided to disband, you cancelled the show,

605
41:01.725 --> 41:03.455
and you went ahead and announced it right away.

606
41:04.395 --> 41:05.495
I put up with it back then.

607
41:06.165 --> 41:08.165
First the car, then the place, and now...

608
41:08.525 --> 41:09.795
you're even doing this.

609
41:10.795 --> 41:11.795
Hey.

610
41:12.195 --> 41:14.205
It's like you were just waiting for us to disband.

611
41:14.805 --> 41:15.805
Do you realise that?

612
41:18.875 --> 41:20.575
It's been ten years. Ten years.

613
41:22.375 --> 41:25.275
All these things that you're getting rid of in a hurry...

614
41:25.415 --> 41:29.085
are things we cherished and built together over ten whole years.

615
41:30.255 --> 41:31.615
How is this so easy for you?

616
41:32.485 --> 41:33.925
How can it be this easy?

617
41:35.125 --> 41:37.095
Hey, okay. Hold on.

618
41:37.395 --> 41:39.895
You both seem pretty worked up, so let's sit down and talk.

619
41:40.795 --> 41:41.995
Let me ask you one thing.

620
41:43.435 --> 41:44.795
Does this really not bother you at all?

621
41:47.405 --> 41:48.605
You have zero regrets?

622
41:54.075 --> 41:55.075
Yes.

623
41:56.545 --> 41:57.545
None.

624
42:02.955 --> 42:04.315
What's there to regret?

625
42:06.885 --> 42:08.154
Shows where we scream our lungs out promoting...

626
42:08.155 --> 42:09.855
just to get barely ten people to show up?

627
42:11.455 --> 42:12.995
This tiny two-room dump?

628
42:14.465 --> 42:16.665
That piece-of-crap car that breaks down every other day?

629
42:17.535 --> 42:18.635
What, exactly?

630
42:20.565 --> 42:21.635
Jun Seo.

631
42:23.535 --> 42:25.075
We failed.

632
42:26.575 --> 42:28.105
Look at us.

633
42:28.905 --> 42:32.075
Stuck in a shoebox, not a penny to our names,

634
42:32.145 --> 42:33.885
just three grown men getting older...

635
42:36.785 --> 42:38.015
We're failures.

636
42:39.085 --> 42:40.325
Total, complete failures.

637
42:42.255 --> 42:43.295
And you have regrets?

638
42:45.095 --> 42:47.465
Do you, really? Seriously?

639
42:51.435 --> 42:53.605
Once we decided to disband, it all hit me.

640
42:57.175 --> 42:59.805
No wonder people laughed at us the way they did.

641
43:02.545 --> 43:04.015
We were truly pathetic.

642
43:08.345 --> 43:10.115
- What? - So I just want to wrap this up...

643
43:12.385 --> 43:13.585
as fast as possible...

644
43:15.755 --> 43:16.995
and start a new life, okay?

645
43:19.355 --> 43:20.565
So please, just cooperate.

646
43:26.635 --> 43:27.965
And cut it out with the regret nonsense.

647
43:30.405 --> 43:31.405
All right?

648
43:36.275 --> 43:38.415
Hey, Kang Tae Gu. Hey.

649
43:38.875 --> 43:42.215
Hey, stop, freeze right there. Hey, you jerk, hey.

650
43:42.385 --> 43:44.015
Hey, Kang Tae Gu. Tae Gu.

651
43:51.555 --> 43:52.555
Jun Seo.

652
43:52.695 --> 43:54.625
Just let it go for now. You know he has no middle ground.

653
44:00.635 --> 44:03.075
Darn it. What am I supposed to do?

654
44:08.805 --> 44:11.815
(Clothing Donation Bin)

655
44:14.715 --> 44:15.715
What's that?

656
44:16.955 --> 44:19.085
- Kimchi fried rice... - Back off, will you?

657
44:19.285 --> 44:20.885
- Why? - Go away.

658
44:21.985 --> 44:23.825
Jun Seo, you're leaving? I made food.

659
44:24.955 --> 44:26.825
Hey, eat before you go. It's all ready.

660
44:29.195 --> 44:30.235
See you later.

661
44:31.095 --> 44:33.565
Hey, have a good one. Watch out for cars!

662
44:36.065 --> 44:37.075
You jerk.

663
44:38.175 --> 44:39.335
Do you have any tact at all?

664
44:40.005 --> 44:41.475
Because of you, I'm stuck in the middle.

665
44:44.345 --> 44:45.475
You didn't make a fried egg?

666
44:45.775 --> 44:48.685
- Why you... Seriously. - What's your problem?

667
44:53.255 --> 44:54.255
Hey.

668
44:55.085 --> 44:57.025
I know when your mind is made up,

669
44:57.695 --> 44:58.995
but consider how he feels.

670
44:59.995 --> 45:01.065
Is that really so hard?

671
45:01.465 --> 45:02.525
I'm only making one for myself.

672
45:03.035 --> 45:04.035
Just try touching it.

673
45:05.165 --> 45:06.635
I should just kill you.

674
45:19.345 --> 45:20.745
You were a social studies teacher?

675
45:21.185 --> 45:22.185
No way.

676
45:22.245 --> 45:23.815
I totally thought you were a musician.

677
45:23.885 --> 45:27.225
I mean, when you sang earlier, I almost completely fell for you.

678
45:28.155 --> 45:29.695
Oh, come on.

679
45:31.355 --> 45:32.395
Well, I mean,

680
45:32.455 --> 45:34.095
back in the day at the school festival,

681
45:34.165 --> 45:35.224
whenever I sang,

682
45:35.225 --> 45:37.295
the girls would threaten to report me.

683
45:37.865 --> 45:38.935
For marriage, that is.

684
45:43.805 --> 45:47.575
Nam Il. Come take a break over here. Just for a bit.

685
45:48.005 --> 45:50.945
- Gosh, it's hot. - Hello.

686
45:51.045 --> 45:53.645
Look at my little freeloaders, here to sponge off me.

687
45:53.715 --> 45:55.985
- Oh, you're here too. Hi there. - Hello.

688
45:56.555 --> 45:57.655
Honey.

689
45:58.255 --> 45:59.255
We're back.

690
46:00.325 --> 46:01.725
Sir, I'm going to take out the trash.

691
46:04.755 --> 46:07.025
Hey, what's his deal lately? Did you guys fight again?

692
46:07.165 --> 46:08.925
The guilty party is acting completely unfazed,

693
46:08.995 --> 46:11.295
and I'm the one stuck in the middle, dying inside.

694
46:11.965 --> 46:14.905
- Yes! It sold. - What did you sell?

695
46:14.965 --> 46:16.535
I've got to go. They want it shipped right away.

696
46:16.605 --> 46:17.735
Boss, I'm taking off.

697
46:18.035 --> 46:21.005
Get out. Go on, you 99 percent gentleman. Get lost.

698
46:22.675 --> 46:23.915
I'm back.

699
46:25.445 --> 46:28.945
- You're back? - Your face is still red.

700
46:29.285 --> 46:30.315
Did you take your medicine?

701
46:32.485 --> 46:34.625
- Where were you? - The skewer place.

702
46:35.025 --> 46:36.725
I just watched some serious drama unfold.

703
46:37.925 --> 46:39.495
Jun Seo and Tae Gu got into a fight.

704
46:39.925 --> 46:42.125
They haven't spoken to each other for two days straight.

705
46:42.595 --> 46:44.435
- Why? - What do you mean, why?

706
46:44.635 --> 46:46.194
Even if they agreed to quit, wrapping everything up...

707
46:46.195 --> 46:48.535
like he was waiting for it would tick anyone off.

708
46:48.905 --> 46:51.674
Earlier, Jun Seo made it so obvious...

709
46:51.675 --> 46:53.505
that he was deeply hurt, radiating it with his entire body,

710
46:53.645 --> 46:55.604
but Tae Gu didn't care at all.

711
46:55.605 --> 46:56.975
If anything, he seemed thrilled.

712
46:58.115 --> 47:00.685
He's so cold-hearted.

713
47:09.155 --> 47:11.895
(Soojung Villa)

714
47:28.505 --> 47:29.875
(Tasty Pizza)

715
47:30.245 --> 47:31.315
I'm back.

716
47:31.715 --> 47:32.915
Don't take your helmet off.

717
47:33.185 --> 47:34.385
You have to head right back out, okay?

718
47:34.445 --> 47:36.045
I only have five minutes left on my shift.

719
47:36.385 --> 47:37.385
- Where is it? - It's nearby.

720
47:37.455 --> 47:38.585
Won't even take five minutes.

721
47:38.655 --> 47:41.685
(Delivery Address: Gag Jirak Green Room, QBN New Hall)

722
48:06.815 --> 48:08.645
Pizza delivery!

723
48:08.915 --> 48:11.115
Hey, guys, let's eat first.

724
48:11.485 --> 48:13.355
- Let's eat first. - Good to see you again.

725
48:13.925 --> 48:14.925
Hey, Tae Gu.

726
48:15.755 --> 48:16.825
Hey, Tae Gu.

727
48:17.255 --> 48:19.455
Are you new here? Why would you order from there?

728
48:19.655 --> 48:22.025
- I'm sorry. I didn't know. - Hey.

729
48:22.425 --> 48:23.465
Good call.

730
48:23.765 --> 48:25.495
Our place makes the best pizza around here.

731
48:26.535 --> 48:27.535
Fastest delivery, too.

732
48:29.975 --> 48:30.975
Tae Gu.

733
48:31.775 --> 48:33.275
Is it true you're quitting comedy?

734
48:33.745 --> 48:35.405
What? Yes, that's how it turned out.

735
48:37.345 --> 48:39.475
Here, I upgraded the sodas on the house.

736
48:40.145 --> 48:41.315
Who's taking care of the bill?

737
48:41.715 --> 48:42.985
Oh, I'll get it.

738
48:48.425 --> 48:50.155
I can't believe him...

739
48:58.895 --> 48:59.965
Here you go.

740
49:00.505 --> 49:01.735
All right, keep up the good work.

741
49:02.205 --> 49:04.335
- Take care, sir. - Goodbye, sir.

742
49:04.405 --> 49:06.535
- Thank you. - Sure, sit back down.

743
49:07.045 --> 49:08.045
Keep at it!

744
49:12.615 --> 49:15.615
(Gag Jirak)

745
50:27.185 --> 50:28.325
I'll give it a try.

746
50:29.185 --> 50:31.055
- I'll head down. - Okay.

747
50:31.655 --> 50:32.655
Okay.

748
50:33.795 --> 50:35.725
- Come on, look quickly. - Okay.

749
50:37.295 --> 50:38.865
All right, let's take it slow.

750
50:40.235 --> 50:41.535
A little more back, just a bit more.

751
50:41.605 --> 50:43.105
- Help him up. Check it. - Okay.

752
50:45.605 --> 50:47.705
- Oh, yes? - Did you check it?

753
51:10.495 --> 51:12.734
Hey, it's been a while since we drank just the two of us.

754
51:12.735 --> 51:13.804
Cheers.

755
51:13.805 --> 51:14.865
Here.

756
51:23.205 --> 51:24.645
What's taking Tae Gu so long?

757
52:11.995 --> 52:14.065
- What are you doing there? - You're back?

758
52:23.365 --> 52:24.505
Because it felt like such a waste.

759
52:26.475 --> 52:28.105
Every single one of these holds meaning,

760
52:29.445 --> 52:33.345
and I thought you might regret it later.

761
52:36.245 --> 52:38.855
They said they would never sell that wig,

762
52:38.915 --> 52:39.985
so I couldn't get it back.

763
52:41.485 --> 52:42.485
And this...

764
52:44.455 --> 52:46.055
I washed it as best as I could,

765
52:46.825 --> 52:48.695
but it was already stained.

766
53:03.675 --> 53:04.675
What are you doing?

767
53:08.985 --> 53:10.615
Who do you think you are?

768
53:13.355 --> 53:15.555
Who are you to keep crossing the line?

769
53:17.955 --> 53:19.195
Isn't that Tae Gu's voice?

770
53:21.025 --> 53:22.395
I told you clearly, didn't I?

771
53:23.325 --> 53:24.535
That we can't turn back.

772
53:25.095 --> 53:26.565
That it's already decided.

773
53:27.505 --> 53:30.405
So why do you keep bothering me like this? Why?

774
53:36.245 --> 53:37.575
Why am I doing this?

775
53:41.515 --> 53:43.115
That's what I want to ask.

776
53:44.185 --> 53:46.155
Why are you doing this?

777
53:47.255 --> 53:48.585
Doing things you don't even mean,

778
53:48.655 --> 53:50.195
hurting others and getting hurt yourself.

779
53:51.195 --> 53:53.025
What on earth are you thinking?

780
53:55.365 --> 53:57.935
- Here we go again. - Tell me...

781
53:58.495 --> 53:59.635
what you're thinking.

782
54:01.035 --> 54:02.965
- Why you're acting like this... - Are you delusional?

783
54:05.135 --> 54:07.145
Get lost before I actually call the cops.

784
54:07.305 --> 54:09.205
- Tell me! - If I do,

785
54:11.315 --> 54:12.745
would you even understand how I feel?

786
54:12.815 --> 54:15.215
Yes, I'll understand.

787
54:18.115 --> 54:19.285
So tell me.

788
54:24.625 --> 54:26.525
Something you couldn't give up for ten years,

789
54:27.225 --> 54:28.695
and you suddenly hate it in an instant?

790
54:29.025 --> 54:32.265
- You expect me to believe that? - Yes. I hate it now.

791
54:33.435 --> 54:34.505
I hate it.

792
54:35.405 --> 54:37.035
It's terrible. I loathe it to death!

793
54:37.105 --> 54:38.475
How could you?

794
54:40.975 --> 54:42.105
You said you loved it.

795
54:44.945 --> 54:46.115
You said it was your dream.

796
54:54.555 --> 54:55.655
Because I felt sorry.

797
55:07.405 --> 55:08.405
I felt so sorry...

798
55:12.275 --> 55:13.435
to the guys.

799
55:32.555 --> 55:33.795
Because of me...

800
55:37.295 --> 55:38.735
Because of me alone...

801
55:42.865 --> 55:44.305
even the guys' lives...

802
55:46.975 --> 55:48.075
Ten years...

803
55:52.275 --> 55:55.745
He dropped out of medical school and cut ties with his family.

804
55:57.715 --> 55:59.115
Look at him now.

805
56:00.585 --> 56:03.055
They say a single choice can determine your whole life.

806
56:06.595 --> 56:08.525
Why are you skewering the green onion first?

807
56:13.195 --> 56:14.235
(Cover Letter)

808
56:14.305 --> 56:18.535
(Resume, Kim Nam Il, Comedy Trio Asura, 10 Years...)

809
56:23.875 --> 56:27.415
(QBN Open Comedian Audition)

810
56:43.965 --> 56:48.065
(10 years)

811
56:54.475 --> 56:57.775
Hey, how much is severance usually?

812
56:58.715 --> 57:00.545
Assuming someone worked for about ten years.

813
57:00.845 --> 57:02.485
Ten times your monthly paycheck.

814
57:03.445 --> 57:05.285
Ten years should add up to quite a lot.

815
57:05.955 --> 57:07.825
Give us our money.

816
57:08.155 --> 57:10.994
You keep saying next time, next time, putting it off.

817
57:10.995 --> 57:12.155
I really will report you.

818
57:12.455 --> 57:13.455
Go ahead, do it.

819
57:13.525 --> 57:15.765
I'll sue you for business obstruction, you punk.

820
57:17.135 --> 57:18.135
Goodness...

821
57:36.085 --> 57:37.455
It was all my fault,

822
57:39.755 --> 57:40.755
so please give us our money.

823
57:43.955 --> 57:44.955
Please.

824
57:54.535 --> 57:56.235
I should've just liked it...

825
58:09.115 --> 58:10.785
I should've just liked it...

826
58:17.125 --> 58:18.895
I should've just liked it...

827
58:21.165 --> 58:22.365
It leaves a stain.

828
58:24.365 --> 58:27.905
A stain, once formed, doesn't wash away easily.

829
58:29.105 --> 58:30.435
The harder you try to erase it,

830
58:31.375 --> 58:32.975
the more worn out it becomes.

831
58:37.915 --> 58:40.685
- Will this stained heart... - I should've just liked it...

832
58:45.015 --> 58:47.855
- Will this worn-out heart... - I should've just liked it...

833
58:52.295 --> 58:54.495
ever get better?

834
58:56.995 --> 58:58.834
I should've just liked it...

835
58:58.835 --> 59:01.935
Is moving on even possible?

836
59:36.865 --> 59:38.105
Is there really...

837
59:39.675 --> 59:40.975
a next step?

838
01:00:04.265 --> 01:00:09.265
(Asura)

839
01:00:56.685 --> 01:00:58.155
The reason Tae Gu refused...

840
01:00:59.055 --> 01:01:01.125
was out of guilt, which I already knew.

841
01:01:04.125 --> 01:01:08.265
(Asura)

842
01:01:08.325 --> 01:01:10.025
Because that's just the kind of guy Tae Gu is.

843
01:01:17.835 --> 01:01:21.745
(Happy Anding)

844
01:01:22.105 --> 01:01:23.675
The ten years we agreed on are up.

845
01:01:24.075 --> 01:01:27.715
- It's your turn now. - I still have three months left.

846
01:01:28.085 --> 01:01:29.945
Do you know where Jun Seo is?

847
01:01:30.315 --> 01:01:32.185
Jun Seo? You can't reach him?

848
01:01:32.685 --> 01:01:34.055
Doesn't he have any friends besides you two?

849
01:01:34.555 --> 01:01:36.055
We're all Jun Seo has.

850
01:01:36.555 --> 01:01:38.755
Tae Gu, I know...

851
01:01:39.755 --> 01:01:42.094
you were lending me a helping hand...

852
01:01:42.095 --> 01:01:43.095
Jun Seo...

853
01:01:43.565 --> 01:01:44.935
so that I could run away.

854
01:01:46.495 --> 01:01:48.065
(Generative AI Used In Select Scenes)

855
01:01:48.135 --> 01:01:49.165
Han Jun Seo!
